xt{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269033 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d3c5f6c-be88-5a7d-88c2-f5f9124aa97d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269033 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317931 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317931 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317931 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a0832f3-44e5-55dc-b0d6-cde9d7754977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318703 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186317931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318703 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318703 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318703 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186317931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318703 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "81013bc8-e699-5fa8-92f3-108172fec02c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319367 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319367 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350203" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319367 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319367 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319367 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4977c738-ef65-5d72-9699-ec8683cb5818" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319367 #edb/ref 1074 "If we let $u=6{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=12x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /2$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\cdot 12x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0-1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319487 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}(\\frac{4}{3})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319487 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319487 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1fb74e6d-27ba-5dab-9bc3-14bcd6aca19d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320651 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320651 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320651 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186319487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320651 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eb778354-29e8-5b6b-9ab2-f74bbde5e184" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320751 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320751 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320751 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320751 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320751 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8cafdf18-d2d8-5608-a2ba-c48b80df9a64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320751 #edb/ref 1074 "If we let $u=2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x),$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{4}^{3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429466 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429466 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once.